    "subject": {
      "system_under_test": "logistic-regression income classifier, facially neutral (RAC1P and SEX excluded from features), 70/30 split, seed 0",
      "data": "folktables ACSIncome \u2014 2018 ACS 1-year person survey, California (US Census) \u2014 378817 rows",
      "data_sha256": "9bcc6ebbb5eabd322eb5d36cae05528ec6a0a4b2a2def8bf1dcde98c02c47d6c"
    },
    "claim": "the system claims to make fair decisions (no adverse impact on protected groups)",
    "verdict": "falsified",
    "finding": {
      "gap": "adverse_impact",
      "effect": "the facially-neutral model reproduces income disparity: disparate-impact ratios of Some other race 0.3065, Two or more races 0.6289, Black or African American 0.7561 and no sex group below the bar, against the EEOC four-fifths threshold of 0.8",
      "detail": "worst: Some other race at 0.3065. The model never sees race or sex, yet its selection rate for the protected group is 31% of the reference group's \u2014 proxy discrimination, because occupation, education, and hours are correlates of the protected group. Female applicants (0.8064) sit just above the bar, which is reported honestly rather than rounded into a catch"
    },
